The regression failed against the old unconditional ownership behavior, then passed after the helper was corrected and connected to the real test adapter. The non-isolated path now refuses registration, and `Drop` gets no cleanup targets even if its metadata is accidentally preseeded; isolated fixture targets still register and drain exactly. I’m recording that red/green result before running the requested full Linux checks and Windows-target type check.
