# Windows store fixture cleanup correction — summary

Corrected the test-build cleanup ownership bug in "'`spikes/001-auth/src/windows_store.rs`:

- Successful test-build writes are recorded for cleanup only when the adapter has an isolated namespace.
- `Drop` issues no deletes for a non-isolated adapter, including when cleanup metadata is unexpectedly prepopulated.
- Cleanup for isolated adapters remains limited to the exact targets recorded for that fixture.
- Added a Linux-executable regression covering registration and cleanup eligibility for isolated and non-isolated states. It uses synthetic metadata only and does not call Windows Credential Manager.

Checks passed: serial `--all-targets` Linux tests (95 library, 11 CLI integration, examples), `cargo fmt --check`, Clippy with `-Dwarnings`, Linux release build, and the isolated Windows store harness all-target/test source check with `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings`.

